Here’s a **realistic, success-driven development roadmap** for **PingMee**, starting from your current stage (Flutter app with splash + onboarding screens) and aiming all the way to launch, user growth, and funding. Each phase includes timelines, milestones, and success goals. Assume you’re working solo or with a small team, full-time or dedicated part-time.

---

## **Stage 1: Core Development (Weeks 1–10)**

### **Week 1–2: User Authentication**

* Email/password + social auth (Google, Apple)
* Secure Firebase/Auth integration
* Store user data in Firestore (name, photo, interests)

### **Week 3–4: User Profile & Interests**

* Profile creation screen (basic info, interests, profile picture)
* Tag-based interest system (e.g., Gaming, Music, Tech)
* Save data to Firebase or Supabase

### **Week 5–6: Ping Creation & Nearby Feed**

* Location permission integration (using `geolocator`)
* Map integration (Google Maps Flutter or Mapbox)
* “Create a Ping” UI with title, tags, location, and duration
* Show pings on map based on user’s radius and interest filters

### **Week 7–8: Ping Acceptance & Chat**

* Join a ping functionality
* Create chat room dynamically when users accept pings
* Implement chat with Stream, Firebase, or Supabase Realtime
* Real-time updates and notifications

### **Week 9–10: Polish + Safety Features**

* Block/report system
* Hide/leave ping
* Profile visibility and privacy settings
* Final polish on animations, transitions, and responsiveness

---

## **Stage 2: Beta & Private Launch (Weeks 11–14)**

### **Week 11: Closed Beta with Friends**

* Test with 5–10 trusted people
* Fix onboarding bugs, map issues, and real-time glitches

### **Week 12–13: Expand Beta Group**

* Run beta in a university or event space
* Track user feedback, behavior, and suggestions
* Add analytics (Firebase, Mixpanel, or Sentry)

### **Week 14: Prepare for Launch**

* Build landing page (with waitlist + feature video)
* App Store and Play Store deployment prep
* Social media + launch assets (logos, screenshots, TikTok, Reels, X posts)

---

## **Stage 3: Public Launch (Month 4)**

### **Soft Launch in 1–2 Target Locations**

* Choose a campus or city to go live in
* Organize a launch event or street activation
* Run early-stage marketing (student ambassadors, local creators)

### **Product Improvements**

* Push bug fixes and polish from launch feedback
* Optimize map and ping performance
* Add quality-of-life features (edit ping, set max participants, reactions in chat)

---

## **Stage 4: Growth & Virality (Month 5–6)**

### **Build Virality In-App**

* Invite friends to pings
* Share pings to socials (with smart deep links)
* “Ping Score” for active users

### **User Acquisition Tactics**

* TikTok videos of real PingMee moments (gather content during beta!)
* Partner with influencers for live ping demos
* Sponsor niche events (e.g., game nights, startup meetups)

### **Track KPIs**

* Daily/Weekly Active Users
* Ping Creation Rate
* Retention (7-day, 30-day)
* Viral coefficient (invites)

---

## **Stage 5: Monetization & Investment (Month 7–9)**

### **Early Monetization**

* Premium Ping features (e.g., pin on map, max visibility, exclusive tags)
* Event pings (for paid organizers)
* Partnered local businesses pings (cafes, coworking, etc.)

### **Startup Investment Roadshow**

* Polish pitch deck (I can help)
* Show traction (DAUs, engagement, viral growth)
* Apply to YC, Techstars, or regional accelerators
* Reach out to angels (networking, Twitter, email, LinkedIn)

---

## **Stage 6: Scaling & Evolution (Month 10–12 and beyond)**

* Hire early team (CTO, product designer, growth marketer)
* Expand to more cities and countries
* Add features like:

  * Voice/video ping intros
  * Group ping communities (like Discord servers)
  * AI interest matching and suggestions
* Build PingMee Web
* Expand analytics dashboard
* Work on partnerships with events, schools, cafes, etc.

